68: | Q57 | An erratum (or any amendment) counts as absorbed only when each fresh attack instance of its class is rejected by the landed instrument and disabling that erratum's guard in-process admits that same instance; a plan-text attack does not establish absorption, and the receipt names both verdict directions and the disabled guard. | erratum/amendment absorption claims and their receipts | M93 `erratum recorded as absorbed without an arm-level receipt` (`corpus/lessons/round-62.md` § Mistakes); C1 matrix (`.ufo/waves/round-62/controls/absorption-hollow.txt:16-27`; `python3 -B verifiers/check_erratum_absorption.py --self-test`). Clause ownership: Q34 owns SOURCES append-only claims; Q35 owns verifier inventory and `SKILL.md` gate-registry/self-test declarations; Q36 owns receipt revision identity; Q56 owns quote/source equality; Q57 owns absorption evidence. Bound: arm-level, not world-level. Bound (round 63, the r62 late seat write `.ufo/waves/round-62/w2/FalsifyC2HonestH1.md`): an honest-fixture arm proves only that its one chosen honest tree passes — r62's H1 fixture passes `check_routed_repairs_v2.py`, while honest variants M-a/M-b/M-e/M-f/M-j of the same repairs fail its R-c/ancestry regexes, so `honest passed 2 of 2` is not an honest-acceptance rate; a population claim needs held-out honest variants.; method credits: tameshi guard-kill/hollow controls (`tameshi-shokunin/corpus/knowledge/guard-kill-closure.md:14-29`), kumitate D49 controls-before-data, kagi self-counts, chousa r16 + game-dev-2d r65-r68 vocabulary; sweep `.ufo/waves/round-62/w2/FalsifyConnector.md` | — |
