75: | Q60 | An artifact cited with a revision must exist at that revision: a receipt or control run against a base B but committed later is cited by its committing rev plus the pinned base B ("committed at <rev>, run against base <rev>"), never as "<path> @ B" — citing committed paperwork at a revision that does not contain it is the M95 class. The check is `git cat-file -e <rev>:<path>`, which exits 128 (nonzero) for a path the revision does not carry; the rule binds the path-claim form only — an output or exit code recorded as "run against base B", with the receipt named bare beside it, is the legitimate pin and is not a violation. Extends Q03 (a record names the commit holding the bytes it describes) and Q58 (a routed defect closes on a counter, not prose); their committed cells are never rewritten. Fix shown able to fail: `git cat-file -e 35d44b4b:.ufo/waves/round-63/controls/C1-do-nothing-v31.txt` exits 128 while the same path at `8c4cefa` exits 0. | artifact citations in lane paperwork (reports, LOG.md, SCORECARD.md, corpus/lessons, receipt headers) and their routed repairs | M95 + M96 — `corpus/lessons/round-63.md` § Mistakes and `corpus/lessons/round-64.md` § Mistakes: the r63 verifier spot-check's defect 2 (`corpus/lessons/round-63-verifier-spotcheck.md:168-173`) routes the r63 report's Before→after lines (`/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/.ufo/reports/round-63/kotoba.md:31-32`), which cite both controls `@ 35d44b4b` while `C1-do-nothing-v31.txt` was added at `8c4cefa` and `C2-before-r62tip.txt` at `cbbee56` (`git log --diff-filter=A`; each control's bytes name base `35d44b4b` — C1 `at: 35d44b4b4dcd…`, C2 `not a tracked blob at 35d44b4b4dcd…` — and `verifiers/check_r63_routed_repairs.py:77` pins `BASE_REV_LITERAL`). Census: ScoutReceiptSweep `<PENDING>`. Executable guard: `python3 -B verifiers/check_r64_routed_repairs.py --rev <rev>`, check 2 `control-revs-named`. | — |
