78: | Q62 | Q14 refinement, not a new rule: a refusal's reason is grounded before it is recorded — a source row or staged claim is refused on an observed fact (a quote absent, an anchor wrong, a scope mismatch), never on an assertion about what the source lacks; a refusal whose reason is false teaches the gate the wrong lesson, and the correction is a new row (the supersede row) plus an appended notice, never a rewrite of the refusal. | source refusals in lessons and SOURCES rows | first-round-69 mistake row naming R68-6/S201 (`corpus/lessons/round-69.md` § Mistakes; evidence: the r68 refusal judged the staged wording a paraphrase, which is verbatim on the page twice) | — |
