97: | Q78 | A size ceiling on `SKILL.md` is a ratchet measured at the freeze, never a promise: the round states the file's bytes, its line count, the number of lines over 120 chars and the longest line, each with the command that measured it, and a ceiling may only move down; a round that lands rows states the headroom it has under the tightest ceiling, and a ceiling already read at its limit (the 600-line box at 600 of 600) cannot absorb a promised row add. A floor that is red at base cannot land; the change is routed. | `SKILL.md` size, and any byte or line ceiling the floors guard is asked to hold | `considerthese/2026-10-26.md` proposal 1 (2026-10-26, at `314e4a1`: 590 lines / 78 569 B / 147 lines > 120 chars / 77 > 300 / longest 1 095 at line 511); measured at the r87 freeze `669f280` — `wc -lc SKILL.md` → `600 86416`, `awk 'length>120' SKILL.md \| wc -l` → `156`, `awk 'length>300'` → `86`, longest `1170` at line 521: the line box is at 600 of 600 while bytes grew 7 847 (10.0 %) since the proposal; `SKILL.md:288` still reads `- [ ] File ≤ 600 lines`; receipt `.ufo/waves/round-87/w1/ScribeLesson/skill-size.txt` | — |
